This page compares zanity with [dddlint](https://github.com/benomahony/dddlint) on the same source files.
Generated by `bench/parity/parity.py` on 2026-10-17, against zanity `7c4a2e5`.

# Rule by rule

Same line means zanity reports it on the tool's line, give or take one. A note identifies deliberate differences.

| Its rule | zanity rule | It fires | zanity fires | Same line | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `alias` | `non-canonical-term` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `alias:module` | `non-canonical-term` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `config:alias-conflict` | `vocabulary-conflict` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) |  |
| `config:duplicate-name` | `vocabulary-conflict` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) |  |
| `config:forbidden-canonical-clash` | `vocabulary-conflict` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) |  |
| `drift` | `name-drift` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `duplicate` | `duplicate-name` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | zanity reports only names another file can use, and not methods of different classes |
| `forbidden` | `forbidden-term` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `forbidden:module` | `forbidden-term` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `test-domain-drift` | `misplaced-test` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `near-synonym` | – | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | No fixture: it comes from an embedding model in `dddlint map`, not from lint. zanity has no embedding features yet |
| `context-outlier` | – | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | No fixture: it comes from an embedding model in `dddlint map`, not from lint. zanity has no embedding features yet |

# Real code

## Recall

Of each tool's findings, how many zanity reports on the same lines with a mapped rule.

| Tool | Its rule | zanity rule | Note | Its findings | zanity too | Recall |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| dddlint | `duplicate` | `duplicate-name` | zanity reports only names another file can use, and not methods of different classes | 555 | 24 | [4%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |
| dddlint | `drift` | `name-drift` |  | 34 | 1 | [3%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |

## Agreement

Of zanity's findings, how many the tool also reports. Low agreement is zanity finding what the tool doesn't, which can be either tool's mistake.

| Tool | zanity rule | zanity findings | Tool too | Agreement |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| dddlint | `duplicate-name` | 24 | 24 | 100% |
| dddlint | `name-drift` | 2 | 1 | 50% |
